   "data": {
    "bull": [
     {
      "text": "Bharti Airtel delivered a 3-year PAT CAGR of 40.1% and revenue CAGR of 14.9% while expanding operating margin from 51.2% to 55.2%.",
      "source_ids": [
       "SCR"
      ]
     },
     {
      "text": "Quarterly revenue grew sequentially from ₹53,982 Cr in Dec 2025 to ₹60,878 Cr in Sep 2026, with PAT rising from ₹8,503 Cr to ₹10,710 Cr over the same period.",
      "source_ids": [
       "SCR"
      ]
     },
     {
      "text": "Operating cash flow over the last three years was 3.75x PAT, indicating strong cash conversion and earnings quality.",
      "source_ids": [
       "SCR"
      ]
     }
    ],
    "bear": [
     {
      "text": "The company carries high leverage with a debt-to-equity ratio of 1.26, flagged as a risk in the financial snapshot.",
      "source_ids": [
       "SCR"
      ]
     },
     {
      "text": "Management's key growth drivers — 4-5% ARPU-led growth over 5-7 years, Rs. 20,000 Cr capex plan (Rs. 14,000 Cr from Airtel), 1 GW data center target for 25% share, and 10% underlying growth after shedding low-margin business — are all unverified against reported financials.",
